dentity Verification\".\n    *   There are two options: \"Employee ID matches ticket\" and \"Manager name matches ticket\".\n    *   Both options have a checkbox next to them.\n*   **Checkbox Status**\n    *   The checkbox for \"Employee ID matches ticket\" is checked.\n    *   The checkbox for \"Manager name matches ticket\" is not checked.\n*   **Additional Information**\n    *   Below the options, there is a message that says \"2 of 4 confirmed - minimum required to proceed\".\n    *   There is also a note that says \"Last 4 digits of phone on file\".\n\n**Summary**\n\nThe image shows a CoreID Admin Console page with a list of options for verifying an employee's identity. The user has checked the box for \"Employee ID matches ticket\", but not for \"Manager name matches ticket\". There is a message indicating that two out of four confirmations are required to proceed, and a note about the last four digits of the phone number on file.\n\n**Detailed Description**\n\n*   **Application and Interface**\n    *   The application is the CoreID Admin Console.\n    *   The interface is a web-based page with a white background and a dark blue sidebar.\n*   **Current Screen and State**\n    *   The current screen is the \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\" page.\n    *   The state of the page is that the user has checked the box for \"Employee ID matches ticket\", but not for \"Manager name matches ticket\".\n*   **Layout and UI Elements**\n    *   The layout is a simple list of options with checkboxes.\n    *   The UI elements include the title, options, checkboxes, and messages.\n*   **Buttons and Menus**\n    *   There are no buttons or menus visible on the page.\n*   **Notifications and Highlighted Areas**\n    *   There are no notifications or highlighted areas visible on the page.\n\n**Extracted Text**\n\n*   **Title**\n    *   \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\"\n*   **Options**\n    *   \"Employee ID matches ticket\"\n    *   \"Manager name matches ticket\"\n*