de the way self-service does?\nThe self-service code exists to authenticate an anonymous claimant with no other proof of identity. Here, identity is established two ways at once: your own CoreID session is already MFA-authenticated and scoped to the Password Reset Admin role, and the caller checklist independently confirms the requester is who they claim to be. Adding a code on top of that verifies nothing new — it would just be an unnecessary step to a channel the caller may not have working anyway, which is usually why the ticket was escalated in the first place.\n\n## CONVERTED OKF STEPS JSON:\n[\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 1,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Confirm the ticket category and extract the requester's employee ID and manager name.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The raw SOP describes a ticket review step, and the 'search_user' function matches this action. The 'solandra' platform is active, and the function aligns with the problem. Required inputs (employee_id) are mappable to entities. Thus, a tool_call was chosen. The 'search_user' function was selected as it directly matches the SOP's requirement to locate the user by employee ID.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"provider\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"search_user\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"employee_id\": \"{{{{entities.employee_id}}}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": null,\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 2,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Verify the caller's identity using at least 2 of 4 identity items (employee ID, manager name, department, last 4 digits of phone).\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The raw SOP describes an identity verification step, and the 'verify_caller_identity' function matches this action. The 'solandra' platform is active, and the function aligns with the problem. Required inputs (user_id, employee_id, manager_name, department, phone_last4) are mappable to entities or prior step outputs. Thus, a tool_call was chosen. The 'verify_caller_identity' function was selected as it directly matches the SOP's requirement to verify the caller's identity.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"provider\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"verify_caller_identity\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"user_id\": \"{{{{variables.user_id}}}}\",\n      \"employee_id\": \"{{{{entities.employee_id}}}}\",\n      \"manager_name\": \"{{{{entities.manager_name}}}}\",\n      \"department\": \"{{{{entities.department}}}}\",\n      \"phone_last4\": \"{{{{entities.phone_last4}}}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.account_found == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 90\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 3,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Generate a temporary password for the locked user and enable the force change at next sign-in flag.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The raw SOP describes a password generation step, and the 'generate_temporary_password' function matches this action. The 'solandra' platform is active, and the function aligns with the problem. Required inputs (user_id) are mappable to prior step outputs. Thus, a tool_call was chosen. The 'generate_temporary_password' function was selected as it directly matches the SOP's requirement to generate a temporary password.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"provider\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"generate_temporary_password\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"user_id\": \"{{{{variables.user_id}}}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.identity_verified == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 4,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Log the resolution audit note and set the ticket status to Resolved.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The raw SOP describes a ticket resolution step, and the 'resolve_ticket' function matches this action. The 'solandra' platform is active, and the function aligns with the problem. Required inputs (ticket_id, resolution_note) are mappable to entities. Thus, a tool_call was chosen. The 'resolve_ticket' function was selected as it directly matches the SOP's requirement to resolve the ticket with an audit note.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"provider\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"resolve_ticket\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"ticket_id\": \"{{{{entities.ticket_id}}}}\",\n      \"resolution_note\": \"Identity verified (2 of 4 checks). Temporary password issued via CoreID. Force-change-at-next-sign-in enabled. No OTP sent - admin-mediated reset per policy.\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.password_generated == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  }\n]\n\n## MANDATORY CoT INSPECTION CHECKS:\nBefore outputting the final verdict, complete these 3 inspection reasoning checks in order:\n\n- **Check 1 (100% Action & Tool Recall & Preservation)**: Verify that EVERY SINGLE automated procedure step described in the raw human text (whether a shell CLI command like `ipconfig`/`chkdsk` OR an API tool action like `unlock_user_account`/`admin_reset_password`) is preserved in the OKF steps. If any automated action or tool call is missing from the OKF steps, you MUST mark `is_faithful = false` and add it to `dropped_commands`.\n  *(HUMAN CONFIRMATION EXEMPTION: Human/verbal/ticket confirmations, user clarifications, and manual admin approval steps are currently PAUSED. DO NOT flag omitted verbal/ticket/user confirmation steps as dropped commands.)*\n  *(GUI SETUP EXEMPTION: GUI setup steps such as \"Open Command Prompt\", \"Press Windows Key\", \"Run as administrator\", \"Open Web Browser\", or opening UI windows are intentionally omitted from executable playbooks. DO NOT flag GUI setup steps or UI window launches as dropped commands.)*\n  *(TOOL PARAMETER MAPPING EXEMPTION: When an automated search or query step maps to a registered API tool whose interface requires a specific input key (such as `search_users` requiring `email`), passing the query entity like `{{entities.email}}` or `{{entities.partial_detail}}` in `comm_inputs` satisfies the step. Do NOT flag other raw search criteria like name or employee ID as dropped commands or parameter inaccuracies when mapping to a catalog tool's defined input parameters.)*\n- **Check 2 (Hallucination Prevention)**: Verify that NO extra CLI commands or fabricated API tool calls were created that were NOT in the raw human SOP text.\n- **Check 3 (Fallback & Parameter Accuracy)**: Verify that fallback commands (`fallback_command`), cross-SOP referrals (`fallback_sop_id`), and tool inputs match the raw text's instructions within the constraints of the registered API tools.\n\n## VERDICT CONTRACT:\n- If all actions are preserved and zero hallucinated commands/tools exist, set `is_faithful = true` and `validation_feedback = \"PASSED FAITHFULNESS INSPECTION\"`.\n- If any actions are missing or fabricated, set `is_faithful = false` and populate `dropped_commands` or `hallucinated_commands`.\n\nOutput a valid JSON object matching the JITFaithfulnessInspectionResult schema.\n"
